how to deal with the doubters and the  haters  so i got a great comment that came in  from one of my newsletter readers love  you guys  a dt who wrote in to say how do you deal  with the doubters and haters how do you  keep your self-esteem high  despite all the criticism this is a  great question to dt and  i call these people the little man you  know the people who  don't believe in your idea who just tell  you all the reasons why something's not  going to work and try to tear you down  the fact is everybody has the little man  in their life  everybody has and when you're trying to  chase your dream when you're trying to  do something big you're trying to do  something important you're trying to do  something that maybe nobody in your  family has ever done before  it's outside the norm then  at the start you're not going to have  all the answers  right it's a dream you're trying to  figure it out you're making corrections  as you go but it's not going to be  perfect you're going to make mistakes  there's going to be holes in your plan  and the little man is a person who sees  all those holes  all those things that you don't have the  knowledge of yet and tells you well  here's all the reasons why it's not  going to work out  where your real friends are the people  who will see those holes  and give you support either in a form of  a solution  here's what you can do here's a problem  you're gonna face and here's how you can  handle it  or just boosting your confidence saying  i believe in you it's gonna work out you  can do this  they don't have to agree with you okay  they don't have to necessarily think  that even what you're doing is right  but if it's your dream and you want to  see this thing through  then your real friends would be the  people who support you no matter what  now it can be hard to eliminate the  people  in your life who don't support you  because sometimes they're really close  but strategy number one is say goodbye  to the little man  now if it's somebody who's not that  close to you it's easy right to stop  talking to somebody who's  an acquaintance is easy what do you do  when it's somebody closer to you  so i want to share two examples from my  my my story  the first is there's a company i work  with it's run by two people business  partners  and one guy  is the little man and this is how i came  up with the name little man  and i showed him some of my stuff and  he's hating on it and he's  hurling insults at me and not telling me  how to make it better  and it got to the point where like this  guy the the email is going back and  this guy's just a drain he's a drain on  my life force  and i can't be around him anymore now  his business partner  i love he he does great by me he's an  awesome individual  if he was stuck in a problem he said  evan i really need your help i would  hop on a plane and fly to him to help  him out  but i have no time for his business  partner and i've eliminated him  from my life and i'm much happier and  able to do much greater things  without him being a part of what i do  another example is even more personal  there's somebody in my extended family  who  who is a little man everything she's  complaining about  is negative is is another drain on you  and doesn't support anything that you do  and became vicious and personal and  degrading  and doing things that i would you know  never imagine people doing other people  especially in your family  and so i decided to eliminate her from  my day-to-day life  and and i haven't seen her in years  and again i've been able to  you know i have much higher  self-confidence and self-esteem  because i'm not around negative people  and that may be hard for you  you know especially if they're close  family you know if it's your parents how  do you tell your parents  i'm not talking to you because you don't  support my dream and i think it's  important to try to explain how  important this is for you  that this is your life that you're  trying to do something to change the  world to make it better this is really  important to you and you really want  their support  because you can't do great things if the  people around you are just trying to  tear you down  so if you can't eliminate somebody from  your life which is the ideal scenario  then at least limit your exposure  on top of that you want to create an  environment that supports you that's  number two create  an environment that supports you you  want to create a routine  you want to be surrounded by people who  build you up you want to consume  stories and media and and information  that builds you up to give you ideas  that give you energy  it's hard enough to  follow your dreams when you have great  people around you  forget about when you have people trying  to tear you down around you but  you want to still have an environment as  much as possible that builds you up so  think about who your friends are think  about the people who you hang out with  do they help build you up  think about the books that you read the  tv shows that you watch the videos that  you consume  the newspapers or websites or whatever  it is that you read  are you surrounded by things that  build you up that give you energy that  gives you creativity  if not then change your surroundings  this is entirely  in your control you can create whatever  world you want your daily routine  what's the first thing that you do when  you wake up every day how do you spend  that first hour of your day  is it doing something that supports you  that builds you up that gives you  momentum that gives you energy  or is it something that just is just  average because again if you're just  being average  you're not going to be able to do  something great so create that  environment think about  who your friends are think about the  music you listen to the books you read  the shows you watch stop wasting time on  facebook and stupid youtube videos  and start consuming stuff that builds  you up that makes you a better  entrepreneur that gives you the  confidence to say  i can do this one of the things that  helped me the most was reading stories  of famous entrepreneurs  famous successful entrepreneurs you look  at how they got started and it was  with nothing most of them with nothing  they didn't have family background  they didn't have a angel investor  venture capitalist dumping millions into  them  they started with nothing they're often  poor broken and  ran out of money but they believed in  themselves they had people around them  who  tried to tear them down tell them why  it's not going to work out but they  believed in themselves  and reading those stories makes me feel  like  i could do the same thing right walt  disney had to go through  all of that crap in his life to become  successful  i could do the same thing you could be  the next walt disney  but you have to create that routine and  that environment that builds you up  and ignore the little man believe  for those of you watching like the video  support me by clicking on the link in  the description  leave a comment let me know what you  think and click on my face subscribe to  the channel thank you so much  i'll see you soon
 

